// Title: Nohup Execution
// Sigma ID: e4ffe466-6ff8-48d4-94bd-e32d1a6061e2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Christopher Peacock @SecurePeacock, SCYTHE @scythe_io
// Date: 2022-06-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.004
// Description: Detects usage of nohup which could be leveraged by an attacker to keep a process running or
//   break out from restricted environments
// False positives:
//   - Administrators or installed processes that leverage nohup
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/nohup/
//   - https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nohup
//   - https://www.computerhope.com/unix/unohup.htm
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_nohup.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/nohup"
